Route the BPE cache counter's AtomicU64 through portable-atomic so the Rust
core builds for 32-bit ARM.

tokenizers 0.23.1 added `static NEXT_CACHE_ID: AtomicU64` to the BPE model
(tokenizers/src/models/bpe/model.rs) to hand every cache a unique id.
`std::sync::atomic::AtomicU64` does not exist on `arm-linux-androideabi`
(armeabi-v7a): 32-bit ARM has no native 64-bit atomic instructions, so std
does not expose the type there at all. That slice therefore stops at

    error[E0432]: unresolved import `std::sync::atomic::AtomicU64`

while arm64-v8a, x86_64 and even 32-bit x86 (which has cmpxchg8b) compile
cleanly -- one 32-bit arch failing and the other passing is the tell for this
class of failure.

The fix keeps the architecture instead of dropping it. portable-atomic offers
the same API with a lock-based fallback where the hardware lacks the
instruction, and its `AtomicU64` is const-constructible, so the `static` still
compiles. Two hunks:

  1. `tokenizers/Cargo.toml` gains `portable-atomic = "1"` as a direct
     dependency of the core crate. It is almost certainly already in the
     build graph -- well-behaved dependencies route their own 64-bit atomics
     through it -- but a crate may only `use` what it declares itself.
  2. `model.rs` imports `AtomicU64` from `portable_atomic` instead of std.
     `Ordering` stays on std: it is a plain enum, and portable-atomic accepts
     the std one.

Nothing else changes; on 64-bit targets portable-atomic compiles down to the
same native instructions, so this is not a performance trade. The alternative
fix for this error -- `excluded_arches: [armeabi-v7a]` in meta.yaml -- was not
needed here because the offending type appears exactly once.

diff --git a/tokenizers/Cargo.toml b/tokenizers/Cargo.toml
index b1d2fa2..ae9478e 100644
--- a/tokenizers/Cargo.toml
+++ b/tokenizers/Cargo.toml
@@ -68,6 +68,10 @@ harness = false
 
 [dependencies]
 rand = "0.9"
+# mobile-forge: 32-bit ARM (arm-linux-androideabi / armeabi-v7a) has no native
+# 64-bit atomics, so std::sync::atomic::AtomicU64 is absent. portable-atomic
+# supplies a fallback so the BPE NEXT_CACHE_ID below builds on armv7.
+portable-atomic = "1"
 onig = { version = "6.5.1", default-features = false, optional = true }
 regex = "1.10"
 regex-syntax = "0.8"
diff --git a/tokenizers/src/models/bpe/model.rs b/tokenizers/src/models/bpe/model.rs
index 6cd2432..a4e2284 100644
--- a/tokenizers/src/models/bpe/model.rs
+++ b/tokenizers/src/models/bpe/model.rs
@@ -6,7 +6,8 @@ use ahash::AHashMap;
 use serde_json::Value;
 use std::borrow::Cow;
 use std::cell::RefCell;
-use std::sync::atomic::{AtomicU64, Ordering};
+use portable_atomic::AtomicU64;
+use std::sync::atomic::Ordering;
 
 use std::collections::HashMap;
 use std::str::from_utf8_unchecked;
